# Project governance

- Read `AGENTS.md`, the requirements, HLD, LLD, and progress checklist before
  planning or changing the system.
- Never treat a proposed value or unchecked checklist item as approved.
- Do not cross a requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, or
  release gate without explicit approval and recorded evidence.
- Verify claims against source, configuration, tests, and current documents.
  Label assumptions and report conflicts.
- Make the smallest coherent approved change. Avoid speculative refactors.
- Never expose secrets, tokens, protected content, signed URLs, or production
  data in code, logs, prompts, tests, or artifacts.
- Update contracts, tests, documentation, observability, and runbooks with
  behavior changes.
- Follow the canonical standards in `docs/engineering/`.
- A task is not done until applicable checks pass and evidence is reported.
